"""Report-decision intervention only: exact prior plans/answers/source preserved."""
from prompts_lsp48 import final_prompt as previous_final_prompt,REPORT_POLICY
from prompts48 import SYSTEM

ROLE_POLICY='''
Make the reporting decision separately from the truth status of the whole candidate. Classify EVERY current condition using condition_roles; preserve IDs, predicates, history and actual uncertainty. Use role=failure_mechanism, trigger_admissibility, path_reachability, behavior_contract, requirement, deployment_observation or impact_magnitude, with necessity=essential, scope_only or frequency_only and an explicit reason. A declaration is a semantic judgment, not a controller-certified fact.
For each claim, provide exactly one report_assessments entry and map its actual finding_indices. Partition ALL unresolved current conditions into essential_unresolved_condition_ids and nonblocking_unresolved_condition_ids. A material API premise, a required producer/consumer connection or a contradiction cannot be hidden as frequency_only. Keep genuinely necessary unknowns essential. Do not move necessary conditions to history merely to emit a warning. Use existing explicit route-revision rules when the explanation is genuinely narrowed; record why.
Ask two different questions: (a) do the implementation and an admissible, explicitly stated input/event schedule establish a concrete wrong operation? (b) has that input happened in an actual deployment, and how often? A supported conditional defect needs (a), not an observed incident for (b). A symbolic but admissible counterexample is enough; do not demand a real user log or actual deployment checkout name merely to show a permitted input. Conversely 'if my unknown external API behavior is true, then failure' is not an admissible witness. Validate or defer indispensable API semantics and path reachability.
Reason using ordinary source-language and data-format semantics. State such semantic bases explicitly as language_or_format_semantics rather than pretending a source span implements the language runtime. Do not demand runtime implementation source for ordinary operators or grammar. Do not invent third-party library behavior, dynamic dispatch, unshown persistence, undocumented payload guarantees or platform mounting rules. Missing observations are not evidence that those premises hold.
Public PR requirements already in this input may establish the intended name, value or behavior, separately from implementation facts. For basis=public_requirement include exact short public_requirement_quotes from Original public PR input; distinguish a normative acceptance target from an author's unverified claim that tests passed or behavior already works. A literal quote is not independent verification of an author's factual claim. Only the frozen repository and environment-bound dependency source pool is available; no internet lookup is available. Use only evidence_ids actually delivered; never cite an unspecified contract as verified evidence.
Use decision=report_conditionally when the failure mechanism, admissible trigger and necessary path/contract are supported but the actual occurrence/frequency is unknown. Write a narrow concrete trigger and impact in the finding and keep nonblocking uncertainty visible. Use decision=report for an unconditional supported defect. Use defer when an indispensable material premise remains unsupported, even if a dramatic hypothetical can be written. Use withdraw only for a refuted cause with the existing source-bound warning/refutation requirements. Emission remains your semantic decision, not an instruction to retain all initial warnings. No defect is assumed to exist in every PR.
mechanism_status, trigger_admissibility, path_reachability and behavior_contract assess the scoped final explanation; not_required needs an explicit reason. deployment_observation is recorded independently and never imputed from a static edge. Every initial warning still has exactly one warning_dispositions entry and both mappings must agree. Never replace a condition's actual unresolved status with supported just to satisfy this schema. A role audit records structural inconsistencies; it neither repairs your final nor proves your interpretation. Keep bookkeeping concise and use the existing final schema for the actual review text and locations.
'''

def final_prompt(*args,**kwargs):
 raw=previous_final_prompt(*args,**kwargs)
 # Replace just the over-broad requirement; all source-location, history and
 # anti-fabrication constraints remain. This is not another model call.
 old='API behavior is a hypothesis until actual implementation or a scoped observation supports it.'
 new='Material third-party API behavior needs supplied implementation/contract evidence or a scoped observation; distinguish that requirement from ordinary language/data-format reasoning and public normative requirements.'
 assert old in SYSTEM
 raw['system']=SYSTEM.replace(old,new)+REPORT_POLICY+ROLE_POLICY
 raw['prompt']+='\n\nApply the condition-role and reporting-decision policy now. Preserve the exact initial warning IDs and source IDs. Return condition_roles and report_assessments alongside the complete REVIEW JSON. The supplied plan and lookup answers were executed previously and are reused without new collection; no new evidence or model call is available after this final.'
 return raw
